a reverse-mode autograd engine in c,
just big enough to train karpathy's microGPT.

ops are recorded on a statically allocated stack that backward walks in
reverse. all memory is allocated statically, TigerBeetle style, and nothing
is allocated after startup. attention is composed from the 12 float64 ops.


correctness by:

- final weights that match karpathy's microGPT to within 1e-11 after 1000
  training steps
- gradient checks against finite differences for every op and the full model
- tests under ASan and UBSan


usage:

    $ make parity

    trained 1000 steps in 0.101s
    passed parity check (max |diff| 5.7e-15)
    inference (random sampled name): kaonle


see also:

- discussion on hackernews: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46285424
- counterpart in lean: https://github.com/sueszli/autograd.lean
- original microgpt implementation: https://karpathy.github.io/2026/02/12/microgpt/
- tigerstyle: https://github.com/tigerbeetle/tigerbeetle/blob/main/docs/TIGER_STYLE.md
